WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.634 --> 00:00:03.970
-As President Trump's ex-lawyer
was headed to jail,

00:00:03.970 --> 00:00:06.406
Trump got definitive,
ironclad proof

00:00:06.406 --> 00:00:08.508
that he did not collude
with Russia

00:00:08.508 --> 00:00:10.677
from the president of Russia.

00:00:10.677 --> 00:00:13.012
For more on this, it's time
for "A Closer Look."

00:00:13.012 --> 00:00:14.480 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:14.480 --> 00:00:17.650 line:0%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:17.650 --> 00:00:19.953
-After Special Counsel
Robert Mueller spent two years

00:00:19.953 --> 00:00:21.687
putting together
a 400-page report

00:00:21.687 --> 00:00:23.723
documenting President Trump's
various links

00:00:23.723 --> 00:00:25.558
to Russian President
Vladimir Putin,

00:00:25.558 --> 00:00:28.360
Trump decided that Friday,
as he was in the middle

00:00:28.360 --> 00:00:31.197
of staging an unprecedented
stand-off with Congress

00:00:31.197 --> 00:00:33.265
over his administration's
handling of that report,

00:00:33.265 --> 00:00:35.568
was the perfect time
to brag about

00:00:35.568 --> 00:00:37.903
his close relationship
with Vladimir Putin.

00:00:37.903 --> 00:00:39.938
-I had a very good talk
with President Putin,

00:00:39.938 --> 00:00:42.375
probably over an hour.

00:00:42.375 --> 00:00:44.310
And we talked about many things.

00:00:44.310 --> 00:00:46.746
-Mr. President, did you address
the election meddling issues

00:00:46.746 --> 00:00:48.848
that came up in the Mueller
Report with Mr. Putin today?

00:00:48.848 --> 00:00:50.249
-We discussed that.

00:00:50.249 --> 00:00:52.585
He actually sort of smiled

00:00:52.585 --> 00:00:54.854
when he said
something to the effect

00:00:54.854 --> 00:00:57.423
that it started off
as a mountain

00:00:57.423 --> 00:00:59.358
and it ended up being a mouse.

00:00:59.358 --> 00:01:00.826
But he knew that,
because he knew

00:01:00.826 --> 00:01:03.596
there was no collusion
whatsoever.

00:01:03.596 --> 00:01:05.598
-And I'm sorry.
Can we go back to this?

00:01:05.598 --> 00:01:06.866
-We discussed that.

00:01:06.866 --> 00:01:09.602
He actually sort of smiled...

00:01:09.602 --> 00:01:12.438
-How did you know
he was smiling? Did you --

00:01:12.438 --> 00:01:13.839
[ Laughter ]

00:01:13.839 --> 00:01:15.542
Did you try to call him
and accidentally hit

00:01:15.542 --> 00:01:18.378
the FaceTime button, Grandpa?
[ Laughter ]

00:01:18.378 --> 00:01:21.213
Putin doesn't seem like the
kind of guy who would FaceTime

00:01:21.213 --> 00:01:24.216
unless he's beaming into
the U.N. on a giant screen

00:01:24.216 --> 00:01:26.885
demanding a billion dollars
or he'll kill James Bond.

00:01:26.885 --> 00:01:28.621
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:28.621 --> 00:01:30.323
But I would definitely
believe --

00:01:30.323 --> 00:01:33.393
I would definitely believe Putin
was smiling when they talked.

00:01:33.393 --> 00:01:35.895
99% of the time
he looks like this.

00:01:35.895 --> 00:01:38.665
Though when he sees Trump,
he lights up like he just heard

00:01:38.665 --> 00:01:40.399
there was a sale on poison.

00:01:40.399 --> 00:01:43.169
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:43.169 --> 00:01:45.838
Now given that Trump and his
Attorney General William Barr

00:01:45.838 --> 00:01:48.174
have repeatedly lied about
the Mueller Report,

00:01:48.174 --> 00:01:50.209
Democrats in the House have
asked for Mueller himself

00:01:50.209 --> 00:01:51.544
to come testify.

00:01:51.544 --> 00:01:53.746
And on Sunday,
one Democrat said

00:01:53.746 --> 00:01:55.281
they'd reached a tentative date

00:01:55.281 --> 00:01:57.517
of May 15th
for Mueller to testify.

00:01:57.517 --> 00:02:00.019
So naturally Trump freaked out
on Twitter.

00:02:00.019 --> 00:02:02.055
-"After spending
more than $35 million

00:02:02.055 --> 00:02:04.657
over a two-year period
interviewing 500 people,

00:02:04.657 --> 00:02:08.661
using 18 Trump-hating angry
Democrats and 49 FBI agents,

00:02:08.661 --> 00:02:10.997
all culminating in a more than
400-page report

00:02:10.997 --> 00:02:14.434
showing no collusion, why would
the Democrats in Congress

00:02:14.434 --> 00:02:16.435
now need Robert Mueller
to testify?

00:02:16.435 --> 00:02:19.105
Are they looking for a redo
because they hated seeing

00:02:19.105 --> 00:02:21.607
the strong "no collusion"
conclusion?

00:02:21.607 --> 00:02:24.344
There was no crime except
on the other side,

00:02:24.344 --> 00:02:26.512
incredibly not covered
in the report,

00:02:26.512 --> 00:02:28.081
and no obstruction.

00:02:28.081 --> 00:02:30.483
Bob Mueller should not
testify.

00:02:30.483 --> 00:02:32.485
No redos for the Dems."

00:02:32.485 --> 00:02:35.287
-Okay, first of all,
"no redos"?

00:02:35.287 --> 00:02:38.090
How is it that Trump always
seems to be 100 years old

00:02:38.090 --> 00:02:40.092
and seven years old
at the same time?

00:02:40.092 --> 00:02:43.329
[ Laughter ]
Watches Fox News, 100.

00:02:43.329 --> 00:02:45.531
Thinks trucks are rad, seven.

00:02:45.531 --> 00:02:46.599
[ Laughter ]

00:02:46.599 --> 00:02:49.502
Thinks Robert E. Lee
is rad, 100.

00:02:49.502 --> 00:02:52.104
Likes McDonald's, seven.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:52.104 --> 00:02:54.374
Second, I thought you said --

00:02:54.374 --> 00:02:56.376
[ Applause ]

00:02:56.376 --> 00:02:58.511
I thought you said Mueller
exonerated you?

00:02:58.511 --> 00:03:00.446
Why don't you want him
to testify?

00:03:00.446 --> 00:03:02.515
"I'm afraid he'll make me look
too innocent.

00:03:02.515 --> 00:03:05.852
I have to maintain some of
my criminal mystique."

00:03:05.852 --> 00:03:07.854
[ Laughter ]

00:03:07.854 --> 00:03:09.121
It really doesn't help your case

00:03:09.121 --> 00:03:10.957
when you tell the cops
you have an alibi,

00:03:10.957 --> 00:03:13.092
but they can't talk to anyone
who can verify it.

00:03:13.092 --> 00:03:15.728
"Oh, Brad can tell you. I was
bowling during the robbery.

00:03:15.728 --> 00:03:18.398
But whatever you do,
don't talk to Brad!"

00:03:18.398 --> 00:03:19.698
[ Laughter ]

00:03:19.698 --> 00:03:21.200
But we need to hear
from Mueller himself

00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:23.936
because Trump and his Attorney
General have spent weeks lying

00:03:23.936 --> 00:03:25.638
about what Mueller wrote
in his report.

00:03:25.638 --> 00:03:27.507
You might remember the report
concluded basically

00:03:27.507 --> 00:03:30.276
what any rational person
who has spent the last two years

00:03:30.276 --> 00:03:32.779
paying attention to the news
expected it might say.

00:03:32.779 --> 00:03:34.580
That even though there was
no criminal conspiracy

00:03:34.580 --> 00:03:36.248
between the Trump campaign
and Russia,

00:03:36.248 --> 00:03:38.451
there were numerous links
between the Russian government

00:03:38.451 --> 00:03:39.885
and the Trump campaign,

00:03:39.885 --> 00:03:42.288
and the campaign expected
it would benefit electorally

00:03:42.288 --> 00:03:44.023
from information stolen
and released

00:03:44.023 --> 00:03:45.291
through Russian efforts.

00:03:45.291 --> 00:03:47.293
So the Trump campaign was
specifically informed

00:03:47.293 --> 00:03:49.529
over and over again that Russia
was trying to help them

00:03:49.529 --> 00:03:52.197
win the election by offering
dirt on Hillary Clinton.

00:03:52.197 --> 00:03:54.400
And over and over again,
the Trump campaign invited

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:55.935
and welcomed that help.

00:03:55.935 --> 00:03:58.137
Most people, if you offered them
a free TV and said,

00:03:58.137 --> 00:04:01.074
"I stole this from Best Buy,"
they'd say, "I don't want that

00:04:01.074 --> 00:04:03.309
and I'm calling the cops,"
but if you offered it to Trump,

00:04:03.309 --> 00:04:06.045
he'd mount it on his wall with
a plaque under it that said,

00:04:06.045 --> 00:04:08.781
"Free TV stolen from Best Buy."
[ Laughter ]

00:04:08.781 --> 00:04:11.450
You might also remember
that when Barr issued

00:04:11.450 --> 00:04:13.653
his infamous four-page
summary of Mueller's report

00:04:13.653 --> 00:04:16.488
in March, he left out
all that information

00:04:16.488 --> 00:04:18.290
and all the evidence
Mueller had gathered

00:04:18.290 --> 00:04:19.625
on obstruction of justice.

00:04:19.625 --> 00:04:21.527
So Mueller,
who never speaks publicly,

00:04:21.527 --> 00:04:23.596
took the extraordinary step
of writing to Barr

00:04:23.596 --> 00:04:25.932
to complain to him that Barr's
letter exonerating Trump

00:04:25.932 --> 00:04:28.600
"did not fully capture
the context, nature,

00:04:28.600 --> 00:04:31.604
and substance of this office's
working conclusions."

00:04:31.604 --> 00:04:35.107
Context, nature, and substance.
So basically, everything.

00:04:35.107 --> 00:04:37.510
Barr even got the author's
name wrong.

00:04:37.510 --> 00:04:39.912
[ Laughter ]

00:04:39.912 --> 00:04:42.949
In fact, Mueller's report
listed 10 separate times

00:04:42.949 --> 00:04:44.549
Trump may have
obstructed justice

00:04:44.549 --> 00:04:45.818
during the investigation.

00:04:45.818 --> 00:04:48.321
Now, one of those 10 instances
involves Trump's

00:04:48.321 --> 00:04:50.289
former White House Counsel
Don McGahn.

00:04:50.289 --> 00:04:52.959
McGahn told Mueller that Trump
had ordered him twice

00:04:52.959 --> 00:04:54.293
to fire Mueller.

00:04:54.293 --> 00:04:55.895
He was so concerned about it,

00:04:55.895 --> 00:04:58.064
he then told
Chief of Staff Reince Priebus

00:04:58.064 --> 00:05:00.065
and even used some
colorful language.

00:05:00.065 --> 00:05:02.135
-According the report,
President Trump ordered

00:05:02.135 --> 00:05:04.569
former White House Counsel
Don McGahn

00:05:04.569 --> 00:05:06.339
to have Mueller fired.

00:05:06.339 --> 00:05:09.242
The President called McGahn
at home and directed him

00:05:09.242 --> 00:05:12.278
to call the acting Attorney
General, Rod Rosenstein,

00:05:12.278 --> 00:05:15.447
and say that the Special Counsel
had conflicts of interest

00:05:15.447 --> 00:05:17.149
and must be removed.

00:05:17.149 --> 00:05:20.753
-It's also the colorful
reporting from this report

00:05:20.753 --> 00:05:24.423
where Don McGahn says
to Reince Priebus,

00:05:24.423 --> 00:05:26.725
which is the third witness
to this incident,

00:05:26.725 --> 00:05:29.928
"The President asked me
to do some crazy [bleep]."

00:05:29.928 --> 00:05:32.465
-It doesn't surprise me
that Trump would tell his aides

00:05:32.465 --> 00:05:34.933
to do crazy [bleep] to interfere
in an investigation.

00:05:34.933 --> 00:05:37.036
He probably tells
them to do crazy [bleep]

00:05:37.036 --> 00:05:39.472
just to pass the time.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:39.472 --> 00:05:41.740
"Rudy, do that thing
where you pull the skin

00:05:41.740 --> 00:05:43.508
all the way back behind
your head.

00:05:43.508 --> 00:05:45.244
Ha-ha-ha-ha-ha!

00:05:45.244 --> 00:05:46.845
Thank you, Rudy.
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:46.845 --> 00:05:49.582
You've cheered me up."
[ Cheering ]

00:05:49.582 --> 00:05:52.818
So Democrats want McGahn
to testify in public.

00:05:52.818 --> 00:05:54.587
Now, he's already testified
to Mueller.

00:05:54.587 --> 00:05:56.121
And Trump and Barr
have both claimed

00:05:56.121 --> 00:05:57.390
that the report
exonerates Trump.

00:05:57.390 --> 00:05:58.991
So you'd think
they'd have no problem

00:05:58.991 --> 00:06:00.493
with McGahn speaking publicly.

00:06:00.493 --> 00:06:02.428
And yet on Friday,
Trump said he might invoke

00:06:02.428 --> 00:06:04.297
executive privilege
to stop McGahn

00:06:04.297 --> 00:06:05.798
from testifying to Congress.

00:06:05.798 --> 00:06:07.633
-Mr. President, did you decide
whether you will invoke

00:06:07.633 --> 00:06:10.503
executive privilege as it
relates to Don McGahn?

00:06:10.503 --> 00:06:13.238
-That'll all be determined
over the next week or so.

00:06:13.238 --> 00:06:14.440
-But you said it was done.

00:06:14.440 --> 00:06:15.741
-But, you know,
I will say this,

00:06:15.741 --> 00:06:19.111
there's been no President
in history

00:06:19.111 --> 00:06:22.381
that has given
what I've given

00:06:22.381 --> 00:06:25.584
in terms of looking at just
a total witch hunt.

00:06:25.584 --> 00:06:28.588
I let him interview the lawyer,

00:06:28.588 --> 00:06:30.923
the White House lawyer
for 30 hours.

00:06:30.923 --> 00:06:32.891
Think of that, 30 hours.

00:06:32.891 --> 00:06:36.428
-Yeah, but do you understand
how bad that sounds for you?

00:06:36.428 --> 00:06:39.132
If your friend went to therapy,
and you said, "How was it?"

00:06:39.132 --> 00:06:42.935
and they said, "I was there
for 30 hours," you'd be like,

00:06:42.935 --> 00:06:46.105
"Damn, you must be dealing
with some crazy [bleep]."

00:06:46.105 --> 00:06:47.406
[ Laughter ]

00:06:47.406 --> 00:06:49.108
Now, all of this
was happening --

00:06:49.108 --> 00:06:51.611
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:51.611 --> 00:06:53.812
All of this was happening
as Trump's former lawyer

00:06:53.812 --> 00:06:55.580
and personal fixer,
Michael Cohen,

00:06:55.580 --> 00:06:57.783
was preparing to report to jail
in part for a crime

00:06:57.783 --> 00:06:59.251
involving the President.

00:06:59.251 --> 00:07:01.587
And in a press conference before
he reported to prison today,

00:07:01.587 --> 00:07:03.956
Cohen hinted that there was
even more to come.

00:07:03.956 --> 00:07:08.727
-I hope that when I rejoin
my family and friends,

00:07:08.727 --> 00:07:12.965
that the country will be
in a place without xenophobia,

00:07:12.965 --> 00:07:17.670
injustice, and lies
at the helm of our country.

00:07:17.670 --> 00:07:21.174
There still remains
much to be told.

00:07:21.174 --> 00:07:24.844
And I look forward to the day
that I can share the truth.

00:07:24.844 --> 00:07:27.112
-Wait, there's more?
[ Laughter ]

00:07:27.112 --> 00:07:28.481
Well, tell us.

00:07:28.481 --> 00:07:30.048
You can't just hint
at something like that

00:07:30.048 --> 00:07:31.717
and then peace out
for three years.

00:07:31.717 --> 00:07:33.051
[ Laughter ]

00:07:33.051 --> 00:07:34.754
It's like if you're about
to go under for surgery

00:07:34.754 --> 00:07:36.288
and your doctor leans over
and says,

00:07:36.288 --> 00:07:38.090
"Okay, we're just going to take
out your appendix

00:07:38.090 --> 00:07:39.992
and then maybe, uh,
some other stuff.

00:07:39.992 --> 00:07:41.627
[ Laughter ]

00:07:41.627 --> 00:07:43.462
You'll just find out what
when you wake up."

00:07:43.462 --> 00:07:45.031
[ Laughter ]

00:07:45.031 --> 00:07:47.599
Cohen keeps dropping hints like
this at his hearing in February

00:07:47.599 --> 00:07:49.868
where he named Trump
as the individual who directed

00:07:49.868 --> 00:07:51.904
the illegal hush money scheme
to cover up the affair

00:07:51.904 --> 00:07:53.339
with Stormy Daniels.

00:07:53.339 --> 00:07:55.674
Cohen hinted that the President
had broken even more laws

00:07:55.674 --> 00:07:57.042
that we're not aware of.

00:07:57.042 --> 00:07:59.912
-Is there any other wrongdoing
or illegal act

00:07:59.912 --> 00:08:03.048
that you are aware of
regarding Donald Trump

00:08:03.048 --> 00:08:04.950
that we haven't yet
discussed today?

00:08:04.950 --> 00:08:06.285
-Yes.
-What?

00:08:06.285 --> 00:08:07.853
[ Laughter ]

00:08:07.853 --> 00:08:10.857
How do you leave something like
that just hanging out there?

00:08:10.857 --> 00:08:13.025
It's like if you're at a party
playing "Never Have I Ever"

00:08:13.025 --> 00:08:15.560
and someone goes,
"Never have I ever...

00:08:15.560 --> 00:08:17.963
fallen into a toilet and gotten
stuck there for 30 days,

00:08:17.963 --> 00:08:19.632
surviving only on toilet water

00:08:19.632 --> 00:08:21.567
until a friend found me
and called 9-1-1

00:08:21.567 --> 00:08:23.369
and they had to lift me out
of the building on a crane

00:08:23.369 --> 00:08:25.037
while I was still stuck
in the toilet

00:08:25.037 --> 00:08:26.572
and take me to the hospital,

00:08:26.572 --> 00:08:28.507
where the toilet was surgically
removed from my butt."

00:08:28.507 --> 00:08:31.043
And then one guy just quietly
takes a sip of his beer

00:08:31.043 --> 00:08:32.778
and goes, "Okay, who's next?"

00:08:32.778 --> 00:08:35.280
[ Laughter ]

00:08:35.280 --> 00:08:36.782
Seriously, can someone --

00:08:36.782 --> 00:08:40.419
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:40.419 --> 00:08:42.121
Can someone maybe
go find Cohen

00:08:42.121 --> 00:08:44.156
and, you know, ask him
a follow-up question?

00:08:44.156 --> 00:08:46.459
We all know where he is.
Before he went to prison,

00:08:46.459 --> 00:08:48.861
he was spotted in Manhattan
all the time.

00:08:48.861 --> 00:08:51.163
And on Saturday, cameras
were literally following him

00:08:51.163 --> 00:08:52.864
down the street paparazzi-style.

00:08:52.864 --> 00:08:54.233
I mean, look at this.

00:08:54.233 --> 00:08:56.668
This guy has more paparazzi
following him than I do.

00:08:56.668 --> 00:08:58.237
One time,
a single photographer

00:08:58.237 --> 00:08:59.739
followed me for 45 minutes.

00:08:59.739 --> 00:09:01.640
When I asked him to stop,
he said, "Oh, sorry,

00:09:01.640 --> 00:09:03.508
I thought you were the guy
from 'The Office.'"

00:09:03.508 --> 00:09:08.548
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:09:12.351 --> 00:09:14.586
So Trump's ex-fixer
reported to jail today.

00:09:14.586 --> 00:09:17.422
And on top of that, we have
more than 400 pages of evidence

00:09:17.422 --> 00:09:19.392
in which it's clear
that the President's campaign

00:09:19.392 --> 00:09:21.060
benefited from
a criminal conspiracy

00:09:21.060 --> 00:09:23.595
to steal information
during the 2016 election,

00:09:23.595 --> 00:09:25.163
and then repeatedly
lied about it

00:09:25.163 --> 00:09:26.932
and tried to stop
the investigation of it.

00:09:26.932 --> 00:09:29.201
We need Mueller and McGahn
to testify,

00:09:29.201 --> 00:09:31.103
and we need Congress
to do its job.

00:09:31.103 --> 00:09:33.238
Otherwise, Trump will have
at least two more years

00:09:33.238 --> 00:09:35.207
to indulge in his
favorite activity --

00:09:35.207 --> 00:09:36.575
-Crazy [bleep].
[ Laughter ]

00:09:36.575 --> 00:09:38.210
-This has been "A Closer Look."

00:09:38.210 --> 00:09:41.881
♪♪
[ Cheers and applause ]

